.TH LINKOD-TOOLKIT 8 "2026" "BSIT 4 - LINKod Group" "LINKod System Administration"
.SH NAME
linkod-toolkit \- Option 1B service lifecycle control scripts for the LINKod application
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linkod-install.sh
[\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-\-source\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR]
.br
.B linkod-service.sh
[\fB\-\-help\fR] \fB\-\-start\fR | \fB\-\-stop\fR | \fB\-\-restart\fR
.br
.B linkod-status.sh
[\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-\-save\fR \fIFILE\fR]
.br
.B linkod-update.sh
[\fB\-\-help\fR] \fIUPDATE_DIR\fR
.br
.B linkod-pause.sh
[\fB\-\-help\fR] \fB\-\-pause\fR | \fB\-\-resume\fR | \fB\-\-status\fR
.br
.B linkod-maintenance.sh
[\fB\-\-help\fR] \fB\-\-on\fR | \fB\-\-off\fR | \fB\-\-status\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B linkod-toolkit
suite provides six Bash system administration scripts implementing Option 1B
(Service Lifecycle Control) for the LINKod Capstone Project 2 web application
(Laravel 13, PHP-FPM, MariaDB/MySQL, and Nginx). It enables administrators to
deploy LINKod onto a clean Ubuntu server, start and stop dependent services in
strict order, monitor ports and resource consumption, safely apply updates with
verified pre-update backups, freeze/resume processes using POSIX signals, and
toggle user-facing maintenance mode.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B linkod-install.sh
Installs Nginx, MariaDB, PHP-FPM, Composer, and Node.js on a clean Ubuntu
server; creates the application database and user using credentials from
\fI/etc/linkod/linkod.conf\fR; deploys the application to \fI/var/www/linkod\fR;
sets least-privilege ownership (\fIwww-data:www-data\fR) and permissions; and
verifies HTTP 200 response.
.TP
.B linkod-service.sh
Starts (\fB\-\-start\fR) and stops (\fB\-\-stop\fR) the LINKod service stack in
dependency order (\fImariadb\fR, \fIphp-fpm\fR, \fInginx\fR). Refuses to start a
second copy if the application is already running.
.TP
.B linkod-status.sh
Reports whether LINKod and its services are running, paused, or in maintenance
mode; displays listening network ports (\fB80\fR and \fB3306\fR); reports
per-process CPU and memory consumption; and outputs system resource metrics via
\fBtop\fR(1), \fBfree\fR(1), and \fBdf\fR(1).
.TP
.B linkod-update.sh
Automatically archives and compresses \fI/var/www/linkod\fR and a database dump
into \fI/var/backups/linkod/\fR, verifies the archive with \fBtar \-tzf\fR,
applies the update from \fIUPDATE_DIR\fR, and verifies HTTP 200 health. If the
post-update check fails, exits with status 1 and prints the exact manual
command to restore the backup.
.TP
.B linkod-pause.sh
Suspends (\fB\-\-pause\fR) the running LINKod worker processes using
\fBkill \-STOP\fR (\fISIGSTOP\fR) so that requests freeze without answering,
and resumes (\fB\-\-resume\fR) them using \fBkill \-CONT\fR (\fISIGCONT\fR).
.TP
.B linkod-maintenance.sh
Switches LINKod into (\fB\-\-on\fR) or out of (\fB\-\-off\fR) Maintenance Mode
using \fIphp artisan down\fR and \fIphp artisan up\fR. Unlike pause mode, the
web server continues answering immediately with HTTP 503 and displays a clear
"temporarily unavailable" message to users.
.SH EXAMPLES
Install LINKod on a clean server:
.PP
.B sudo ./linkod-install.sh
.PP
Start and check the status of LINKod services:
.PP
.B sudo ./linkod-service.sh --start
.br
.B sudo ./linkod-status.sh
.PP
Apply an update directory (auto-backs up and verifies first):
.PP
.B sudo ./linkod-update.sh /home/justin/it123-linkod/demo-updates/broken-update
.PP
Freeze and resume application processes:
.PP
.B sudo ./linkod-pause.sh --pause
.br
.B sudo ./linkod-pause.sh --resume
.PP
Enable and disable user-facing maintenance mode:
.PP
.B sudo ./linkod-maintenance.sh --on
.br
.B sudo ./linkod-maintenance.sh --off
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/linkod/linkod.conf
Root-owned configuration file (permissions \fB600\fR) storing database
credentials and directory paths.
.TP
.I /var/www/linkod
Deployed LINKod Laravel application root directory.
.TP
.I /var/backups/linkod
Directory (permissions \fB700\fR) storing dated pre-update \fI.tar.gz\fR
archives and SQL dumps.
.TP
.I /run/linkod.lock
Runtime lock file preventing duplicate service starts.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Operational, privilege, service, or post-update verification failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line option or missing required argument.
